      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Class 4 impact-resistant shingles provide the highest level of protection against severe weather, making them a smart investment for Utah's high winds, winter freeze-thaw cycles, and occasional hail.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "provide the highest level of protection against severe weather"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "What is a Class 4 Rating?"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "UL 2218 Test: Shingles must survive a 2-inch steel ball dropped from 20 feet without cracking or splitting on the underside."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Material: They use polymer-modified asphalt (like SBS) that gives them rubber-like flexibility to absorb sudden impacts rather than snapping."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Benefits in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Wind and Debris: Utah wind corridors and mountain elevations subject roofs to high winds and wind-driven debris. Class 4 products hold granules better and slow down weathering."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Insurance Discounts: Many insurance companies operating in Utah offer annual premium discounts (often 5% to 28%) for homes equipped with Class 4 roofs. Check with your specific carrier before buying."
          }
        ]
      },
